1mm mouse brain volumetric multiplexing

One 1 mm thick mouse brain slice imaged in 3D over sequential protein staining rounds
on a light-sheet microscope (3.6x / NA 0.2 detection, 1.8 um/px in x and y, 1.273 um z step).
Each volume is destriped, deskewed and stitched (full stitched field, not cropped).
Volumes are not registered across rounds.
Files are multiscale OME-Zarr (NGFF 0.4, 6 resolution levels, 2x2x2 mean downsampling).
Each file has 2 channels: channel 1 is the marker (stain label ends in Protein), channel 2 is
Histone H3 protein (488 nm excitation) from the same acquisition, in the same voxel frame,
included so volumes from different rounds can be registered to each other.
Files with stain label Background561 / Background639 are unstained (blank) channels from a
round with no markers, provided as background / autofluorescence references.
